Z||000001||fierosound||02-11-2000||05:53 PM||||I hate EBAY because you can't get any deals there because of the "bidding war" mentality that some people get.  Because of that, the only winners are the sellers.  I doubt very many people find a real bargain, unless it's something nobody wants.<P>I wanted a car cover fitted for a Fiero GT and a used one showed up on EBAY.  I was first bid at $25, and over a few days pushed it to $40, then $50 as others had bid as well.  Within two more days it shot to within $20 of the price of a new one.  The idiot who bid that price is welcome to it!||||reg||13
Z||000002||Sage||02-11-2000||06:18 PM||||Tom once said he sold mirror switches for ten bucks & shipping, that seems more inline for a used part.  Ebay has gotten outaline for just the reason stated above. (That's why I thought I might have a chance of selling the 86GT there, but it really IS a bargain at $2,400, even with everything it needs done to it!)Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-11-2000||07:21 PM||||I don't even look at the online auctions any more. I noticed some time ago, both for the car and in electronics, that there are no deals and plenty of suspicious behavior. ((Rarely does any remotely current electronic device sell below retail prices I can get on the street.))||||reg||1
