Z||000005||ggarsk||02-11-2000||08:05 PM||||I've gotten a lot of good deals on E-Bay. Of course I'll wait till the last minute to bid....if it's within what I want to spend I'll bid if not I'll wait till another one comes up. I've noticed that even buying things from members the prices vary for the same item. But it really boils down to how bad you need or want the item.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||02-11-2000||09:39 PM||||Amen, monkeyman!<P>I can definately say that I did have a good experience with a guy on Yahoo, tele52, teleman52, something like that.  I bought a set of Aura Pro Bass Shakers from him for $90 less than retail, items were new, the guy responded to every one of my emails within 24 hrs, and I received my package within 1 week of mailing payment.  But $40 for a $5 Pick and Pull part? Some peoples kids!||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||02-11-2000||10:16 PM||||The mirror switch is $31.99 and the pwr window switches are only $4.70 ea.  So you can get this brand new for about what the asking price of his junk is!  <BR>I quickly file those who frequently post stuff like this on ebay into my "do not ever buy from" bin.  Its obvious that it has become a place to either exploit those less knowlegable about the value of an item, or benefit from the ego bidders who seem to have nothing better to do. <P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierosound||02-12-2000||01:54 AM||||Stimpy<P>Aura Pro Bass Shakers are one of those items that "didn't sell".  I'm not even sure they make them anymore.  I was in a car audio shop before Xmas to look around, and they had a pair they wanted to get rid of because nobody wanted them.  They said they'd give them to me below cost to get rid of them..<P>As I said, you can only get a deal on an item nobody else wants...<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||02-12-2000||02:03 AM||||This isn't Fiero related.. and I think I've told this story before.. but I found an ebay auction once about a star wars ep1 poster.. the theater teaser poster, with anakin casting the vader shadow. The auction said they were rare, and I was looking for one.. I ended up paying $30 for it.. then I found an identical one at wal-mart the next day for $5.. it was a canadian reproduction and the one I bought was an actual lucasfilm one.. but still.. the poster looks the same! so I put the wal-mart one up on my wall and kept the other one in the cardboard shipping tube so it'll stay in good condition..<BR>I haven't seriously bid on any ebay auctions since.||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||02-12-2000||09:15 AM||||Buyer beware on eBay. You can find some great deals and you can get ripped off too. I was determined to buy one of those limited edition Pink Floyd "Pulse" CDs that had a working flashing LED light in the case. I bid on a dozen of those suckers, but refused to spend more than $20 including shipping. People were consistantly bidding over $40 for them, even though my price book stated the value was only $25. I about gave up, but finally bought one that nobody was bidding on for $12 (plus another $3.20 for priority mail shipping). It turned out to be brand new and still in the sealed wrapper, plus the LED light was still blinking too! Go figure! Gotta be patient.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Robert||02-12-2000||10:34 AM||||I have learned to look up done deals on the same item, to see what they are really selling for, before I bid.  I once paid to much for a digital camera, but never again.  My ebay story is I bought a table saw at Home Depot that I only needed for a one time project, so I put it up for auction. It sold for $30 more than it cost me. :-)||||reg||1
